// libs/metal — OMNI's renderer contract: window/frames/draw/input/
// text/image/offscreen verbs (~50 public tors) over a platform pixel
// backend. Platform bodies live in gated parts — index.<os>.kz joins
// only under its build flag, so the unselected body is dormant bytes:
// never parsed, never emitted, zero cost. That deadstrip-at-parse is
// the part system's whole claim, and this module is its stress test —
// index.macos.kz is ~3000 lines of ObjC/Metal that must not exist in a
// koru-native build, and index.koru-native.kz is the freestanding
// rasterizer over koruos/surface that replaces it.
//
// Decl surfaces ride the parts (phantom types *Window<opened|active>,
// *Frame<frame>, *Surface<ready> are platform-typed) — a consumer sees
// whichever body's decls merged; the signatures are identical by
// contract.

~[build == macos]part macos
~[build == koru-native]part koru-native
